 - [The driver wires memory tens of thousands of times a second with residency sets on the queues](../../../docs/reference/frame-rate.md#the-driver-wires-memory-tens-of-thousands-of-times-a-second-with-residency-sets-on-the-queues): resolved by naming the residency sets on each command buffer; the driver's cause is open. 0 of 20 launches in the state on a 16 GB M4 and 0 of 4 on a 16 GB M2, against 10 of 20 and 5 of 5.
+
+## Controller layout overlays (`DM_PAD_LAYOUT`)
+
+- The game draws its in-game button icons from two places: its own `Font/External.Nin_Ounce_NVN2.bfotf.zs` (an XOR-obfuscated OpenType CFF font with the Nintendo Switch PUA glyphs `U+E0A0..U+E0F2`) and the pause-menu controller screen's `UI/Controller/Controller.Nin_Ounce_NVN2.bntx.zs` (35 ASTC 8×8 sRGB textures: `Controller_Pro{0,1}`, `Controller_Console{0,1}`, `Controller_Grip{0,1}`, and 29 `Line_*` callout overlays).
+- [`scripts/oot_pad_overlay.py`](../../../scripts/oot_pad_overlay.py) (with [`dm/tools/oot_pad_overlay.m`](../../tools/oot_pad_overlay.m) and the reference renders [`controller_dualsense.png`](controller_dualsense.png) and [`controller_xbox.png`](controller_xbox.png)) builds `overlay_playstation/` and `overlay_xbox/` from the extracted RomFS during packing (`scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py` and `dm/ios/tools/build_ipa.sh`), replacing the CFF glyph outlines and re-encoding the 35 ASTC textures so `DM_PAD_LAYOUT=playstation` and `DM_PAD_LAYOUT=xbox` swap both the HUD button icons and the pause-menu controller diagram + callout lines.
