diff --git a/docs/agents/symptoms.md b/docs/agents/symptoms.md
index b09f1995..8eb0be8b 100644
--- a/docs/agents/symptoms.md
+++ b/docs/agents/symptoms.md
@@ -350,6 +350,7 @@ One line per symptom in the [subsystem references](../reference/): what you see
 - `[RED] sf: the game connects to service nfp:user itself`, then `game called nn::diag abort: Result 0xe15` under the game's own initialization (`main+0x115deb0`). → [`nfp`'s extended application area](../reference/services.md#nfps-extended-application-area)
 - selecting amiibo initializes `nfp`, then the game connects to the unserved `nfc:user` service and aborts in `nn::nfc::Initialize`. → [NFC initialization beside the amiibo library](../reference/services.md#nfc-initialization-beside-the-amiibo-library)
 - `game called nn::diag abort: Result 0, call site sdk+0x13ce58` in the middle of play, from `nn::os::TryWaitSystemEvent` on an event that was never set up (backtrace `main+0x1fb9920` in Tears of the Kingdom 1.4.3). → [The amiibo library's state before Initialize](../reference/services.md#the-amiibo-librarys-state-before-initialize)
+- every amiibo scan finds nothing: `nfp: GetTagInfo and other operations that need an amiibo tag → no tag found`; no amiibo feature (Breath of the Wild's amiibo rune, a figure's saved data) can be used. → [Virtual amiibo (`DM_AMIIBO`)](../reference/services.md#virtual-amiibo-dm_amiibo)
 - abort in `nn::sm::Initialize` under `nn::hid::VibrationNode::Update`. → [Vibration values flushed by the SDK's vibration graph](../reference/services.md#vibration-values-flushed-by-the-sdks-vibration-graph)
 - at boot, `[RED] sf: the game connects to service hid itself`, then `CRASH sig=11 addr=0` in `hid::detail::EndPermitVibrationSession` (`sdk+0x3526bc` in SDK 9.4), under `hid::EndForcedVibrationSession`. → [Forced vibration sessions](../reference/services.md#forced-vibration-sessions)
 - with rumble on, `[RED] sf: the game connects to service hid itself`, then `CRASH sig=11 addr=0` in `hid::detail::IsVibrationDeviceMounted` (`sdk+0x24254c` in SDK 7), under `hid::IsVibrationDeviceMounted`. With rumble off in the host's settings the game never asks. → [Whether a vibration device is mounted](../reference/services.md#whether-a-vibration-device-is-mounted)
diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 79796cda..c9ae977c 100644
